| =====================================================================
|  BoxAssist.mac  -  Rogue drives the Shaman box  (SoR, 2-box)
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------
|  Run this ON THE ROGUE. It tells your boxed Shaman to assist the Rogue's
|  target and keep slow + malo applied, so you never have to alt-tab for it.
|
|  REQUIRES a comms plugin on BOTH characters:
|     * MQ2DanNet   (commands shown below use /dgt = DanNet "tell group")
|     * or MQ2EQBC  (swap /dgt for: /bct ShamanName //<command>)
|
|  Bind it:   /bind LeftAlt+3 /mac BoxAssist
|  Stop:      /endmacro
| =====================================================================

Sub Main
    | ---------------------- CONFIGURE ME ----------------------------
    /declare ShamanName      string outer Shamanname        | <-- your Shaman's name
    /declare SlowSpell       string outer Turgur's Swarm     | highest slow you own
    /declare MaloSpell       string outer Malosenia          | highest malo you own
    | Comms style: "dannet" or "eqbc"
    /declare Comms           string outer dannet
    | ----------------------- END CONFIG -----------------------------

    /echo \ag[BoxAssist] Driving Shaman (\ay${ShamanName}\ag). /endmacro to stop.

    :loop
    /doevents

    /if (!${Target.ID} || ${Target.Type.Equal[PC]} || ${Target.Type.Equal[Corpse]} || ${Target.PctHPs} <= 0) {
        /delay 10
        /goto :loop
    }

    | Send the Shaman to our target, then have it slow + malo.
    | The Shaman only recasts if its target isn't already slowed/maloed -
    | that buff check runs on the Shaman side via /casting's duplicate guard
    | (or your Shaman bot routine handles it entirely; see note below).
    /call BoxCmd "/target id ${Target.ID}"
    /delay 3
    /call BoxCmd "/casting \"${SlowSpell}\""
    /delay 5
    /call BoxCmd "/casting \"${MaloSpell}\""
    /delay 5

    | Re-check roughly every 30s (don't spam the Shaman)
    /delay 300
    /goto :loop
/return

| --------------------------------------------------------------------
Sub BoxCmd(string Cmd)
    | Cmd should already begin with a leading slash, e.g. "/target id 123"
    | NOTE: the exact "make a peer run a command" verb varies by plugin/version.
    |   * EQBC:    /bct <name> //<command>   (confident)
    |   * DanNet:  /dex <name> <command>     (verify; some builds use /dexecute,
    |              /dge, or /dgga for group-wide execute - check /dnet help)
    /if (${Comms.Equal[eqbc]}) {
        /bct ${ShamanName} /${Cmd}
    } else {
        /dex ${ShamanName} ${Cmd}
    }
/return

| ---------------------------------------------------------------------
| NOTE: Slow/malo casting logic lives mostly on the SHAMAN side. The
| cleanest setup is a small heal/slow routine ON the Shaman (Very Vanilla
| MQ ships class routines) and this macro just keeps the Shaman targeting
| your kill target. If you use a full Shaman bot routine, you may only need
| the "/target id" line here and let the Shaman handle slow/malo/heals.
| See docs/05-shaman-box-coordination.md.
| ---------------------------------------------------------------------
